From 383dd65e069c02b538eac9671dbc9728468eb36e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: heresy <heresy@local>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 18:23:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1019/1259] The song's key beside the title
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

HERESY 1019. A narrow Key list on the title's line (minor and major keys, the
usual spellings). With a score in the form it shows the score's key, and a
choice moves the score there. With no score yet the choice waits (a dashed
frame): the next score that arrives — a plan, a Retake, a transcription — is
moved to it once, with a word saying so. In Full mode the model writes its
own score and may ignore a key named in the style; this makes the key the
song is in a choice of the user's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
